---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy">
  <section class="section paper">
    <article class="container narrow prose">
      <p class="eyebrow">YOUR INFORMATION</p>
      <h1 class="page-title">Privacy & enquiries.</h1>
      <h2>What stays in your browser</h2>
      <p>
        The enquiry list and item notes are stored in your browser’s localStorage. Clear the list or
        browser site data to remove them. On the interactive GitHub Pages showcase, submitted preview
        enquiries also stay only in that browser so the client can test the lead-desk experience. On
        the production Hostinger deployment, submitted contact and requirement details are stored for
        SHK so the team can respond and manage follow-up.
      </p>
      <h2>Sending a requirement</h2>
      <p>
        The form first submits your enquiry to SHK's lead desk. It can then generate a WhatsApp
        message containing the same requirement for you to review and send. If you opt in and SHK's
        WhatsApp Business messaging is configured, SHK may also send an acknowledgement and
        catalogue link using that service. WhatsApp's own privacy terms apply.
      </p>
      <h2>Drawings and attachments</h2>
      <p>
        When SHK's secure attachment storage is configured, supported drawings, photos and documents
        selected in the form are uploaded with the enquiry and are available only through the
        authenticated SHK lead desk. If that storage is unavailable, the site keeps the filenames in
        the enquiry and asks you to attach the files manually in WhatsApp.
      </p>
      <h2>Analytics and hosting</h2>
      <p>
        This build uses no analytics scripts or advertising cookies. The hosting provider may
        process ordinary request logs when the site is deployed.
      </p>
      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p>
        Contact <a href={`mailto:${site.contact.email}`}>{site.contact.email}</a> about information
        you share with SHK.
      </p>
    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
